{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795029265758901716,"compiled_state":{"alias":"starving-sphalerite-skua","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"1aeb88c40be7627626d8a3fef44c965235f2210893d4f03627268cf6297adfa1","event_uuid":"47c1b7e0-79c1-46d0-9241-c04653d87600","position":{"commit_sha":"cb70e81da163e277aabfee84eef8408c3dcd1457","position":"1795029251512550065-47c1b7e0-79c1-46d0-9241-c04653d87600"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"862db962c5cca60aa67ef2a74eb1feaac91c2cce85507aeaf24e5f98618549cd","event_uuid":"ad3127f4-6fee-43da-aff2-ecb0a556ec4c","position":{"commit_sha":"d3a5b14ca000dc2931df3ca03cd07e04974aee8c","position":"1795029260959868843-ad3127f4-6fee-43da-aff2-ecb0a556ec4c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9f1846b11952bab0c6da4292eb2d12767982a67a878082a560945fafeb4d9608","event_uuid":"aeba47ed-b415-465b-86e2-ae0ebe994626","position":{"commit_sha":"ecd635cae26e2882712d316f03c9e109fcec6ba5","position":"1795029265758901715-aeba47ed-b415-465b-86e2-ae0ebe994626"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795029251512550065,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ad3127f4-6fee-43da-aff2-ecb0a556ec4c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"84f6-ac03-4044-44d5"},{"link_uuid":"aeba47ed-b415-465b-86e2-ae0ebe994626","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"536b-8930-b922-4063"}],"description":"## Observation\nWith the tame-melodious-veery performance fix, enforced `verify-identity --all` (`REBAR_IDENTITY_REQUIRE_AUTHENTICATED=1`, no `enforce_since`) now completes on a fresh no-remote TMPDIR clone of `origin/tickets` b878d77e28d (310,079 commits) in 26 min 7 s. It exits 1:\n\n`42612 verified, 874 unsigned, 0 unknown-author, 7007 bad-signature, 0 key-not-valid-at-era (50493 event(s) in scope)`\n\nAll 7,007 bad-signature verdicts are SNAPSHOT `authorship_ledger` entries (1,018 tickets); no live event is bad-signature. This is the ORIGINAL, un-reclaimed history, so it is not a reclaim defect.\n\nLedger composition on that clone (44,311 entries), grouped by the SSHSIG public key embedded in each signature (sha256 prefix of the key blob) and by whether compaction recorded `signer_pubkey`:\n- key 3d4e271c8a89 (on identity 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d's keyring, added 1784000818…): 35,403 set, 1,301 null\n- key a060aace07c3 (on the keyring, added 1788820763…): 2,600 set, 19 null\n- key 6e2a8414bf53: 2,557, all null — NOT on any keyring record of 594c\n- key 61689bf468f5: 2,430, all null — NOT on any keyring record of 594c\n- key 0a2a4ec106e4: 1 set\n\n`_verify_signed` in `src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py` returns `bad-signature` for any ledger entry whose `signer_pubkey` is null, before trying a verify. So two classes are mixed:\n1. ~4,987 entries signed by two keys that the author identity's keyring never recorded (genuinely unverifiable against in-band keys; which hosts held those keys is not established).\n2. ~1,320 entries signed by keys that ARE on the keyring but recorded null at compaction (a random sample of 40 null entries: 4 verify against the current keyring via `identify_signer`, 36 do not). Likely compaction ran where the key was not yet on the keyring; not established.\nThe remaining ~700 bad-signature verdicts among `signer_pubkey`-set entries are not yet broken down.\n\n## Why it matters\nEpic polite-antivirus-bedbug's operator hold requires an enforced `verify-identity` that PASSES on the rewritten history before publication. It cannot pass on the rewritten history while it fails on the original. CI runs with `enforce_since` set, which grandfathers pre-anchor events, so the CI lane is not affected today.\n\n## Not established\n- Where keys 6e2a8414bf53 and 61689bf468f5 come from, and whether they should be registered on identity 594c (a keyring change is an operator decision about trust).\n- Whether the intended acceptance for the reclaim hold is \"enforced with the committed `enforce_since`\" or \"enforced with no boundary\".\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The origin of each bad-signature class is identified with evidence (keys and compaction hosts).\n- [ ] The remedy (keyring registration by the operator, re-identification of signers at verify time, or a documented grandfather boundary) is decided by the operator and implemented.\n- [ ] Enforced `verify-identity --all` on a fresh clone of origin/tickets reports 0 enforced not-verified events under the decided boundary.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","536b-8930-b922-4063"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["identity","verify-identity"],"ticket_id":"df01-290f-89a2-4ce8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Enforced verify-identity fails on the current tickets history: 7,007 SNAPSHOT ledger entries classify bad-signature","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["47c1b7e0-79c1-46d0-9241-c04653d87600","ad3127f4-6fee-43da-aff2-ecb0a556ec4c","aeba47ed-b415-465b-86e2-ae0ebe994626"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795029265758901716,"uuid":"73b880dc-1b3d-45f1-a94d-05b9233432ed"}